# [[.ProjectName]] storefront

This Nuxt storefront foundation is generated deterministically by Scaffold Agent.
It provides the shared SSR shell and bounded backend boundary that later catalog,
cart, checkout, order, account, and marketing capability packs extend.

## Runtime

- Node.js 24.11 or newer
- `SCAFFOLD_API_BASE_URL`: server-only backend base URL; defaults to `http://127.0.0.1:8080`[[if and .Catalog .Tenancy]]
- `SCAFFOLD_ORGANIZATION_ID`: required server-only organization identifier for public catalog reads[[end]]

The browser calls `GET /api/storefront/status`. Nuxt calls the generated backend
`GET /readyz` with a two-second deadline and never exposes its address or failure
details to the browser.[[if .Catalog]]

The catalog capability adds server-rendered product list and detail pages. The
browser still calls only same-origin Nuxt endpoints; Nuxt validates pagination
and identifiers before forwarding bounded requests to the generated backend.[[end]][[if .Commerce]]

The commerce capability adds cart, checkout, customer order history, and return
pages. For local demonstrations only, set `COMMERCE_SANDBOX_ENABLED=true` on the
backend and `NUXT_PUBLIC_COMMERCE_SANDBOX_ENABLED=true` on the storefront. Both
flags are disabled by default.[[end]]

## Commands

```bash
npm ci
npm run lint
npm run test
npm run typecheck
npm run build
npm run format
```

Do not place API tokens, payment secrets, backend credentials, or private customer
data in `runtimeConfig.public`, client components, browser storage, or source files.
